The assassination of the high chief Tupua Tamasese Lealofi III in the city occurred during the struggle for independence organized by the Mau movement.
Due to Cleveland's two rivers flowing around it, it has many beaches. The most famous ones are located in three districts.
The Northern Beaches of the Northern Harbors district are located in the Pacific Ocean, stretching from the northern Long Bay to the southern Devenport.
They are sandy beaches, almost like a shelter from the sun, with the shade of coconut palms often falling over them.
Tamaki Drive beaches are located on the Waitemata Harbour, along the prestigious suburbs of Mission Bay and Saint Heliers in Central Auckland.
These are family beaches with sometimes crowded, row-like shops along the shore. Swimming is safe.
